==================================================
  HELP
==================================================
 WHAT THE PROGRAM DOES
   Builds a table of y(x) for x = start, start + step, start + 2*step, ... up to the end.

 INPUT DATA
   Start value   where the table begins        any number, e.g. -2
   End value     where the table ends          not smaller than the start, e.g. 4
   Step          how much x grows in each row  greater than 0, at most 1000 rows
   Parameter n   the last number the formula counts up to (1, 2, ... n),
                 whole number from 4 to 1000. The bigger n, the bigger the results.
   Use a dot for decimals: 0.5, not 0,5

 HOW TO USE
   1. Enter data from the keyboard (option 1) or load it from a file (option 2).
   2. Choose option 3 to see the table. You can save it to results.txt.
   If a value is wrong, the program explains why and asks again.

 FILE FORMAT
   4 numbers separated by spaces, in this order: start end step n
   Example: -2 4 1 5        (default file name: input.txt)

 SPECIAL RESULTS IN THE TABLE
   not defined   x = 0: the term 1/(2x) would divide by zero
   too large     the value is bigger than the computer can store
   6.54826e+07   a big number: 6.54826 * 10^7

 Press Enter to continue...
